From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: screenshots for Linux apps

The Screenshot portal's NickelOS backend (xdg-desktop-portal-nickel) asks
ChromeOS's "share your screen" picker which screen or window an app may
have (NickelScreenCastChoose, 0022), then has it copied once:

- NickelScreenCastShot(source, frame buffer, width, height): copies the
  screen's or window's layer once into the backend's shared memory, BGRx,
  answering whether it did. It waits until nothing on the screen is
  animating (at most a second), so the picker that chose the source has
  faded out and the screenshot doesn't show it, and shows no "sharing
  your screen" notification: the user just said yes in the picker, and
  nothing goes on being shared. The buffer must be the frame's size.

